 "\nThe precise meanings of the functions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", "[", "...", "]"}], "  ", "and", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "...", "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
 ", etc. are relevant.  All functions pass through the same universal \
evaluation procedure.  Functions behave differently ",
 StyleBox["only",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " because they are exposed to different parts of the universal evaluation \
procedure.  This control is determined by each function's attributes like \
HoldAll, HoldRest, Listable etc. and control functions like Unevaluated[...], \
Hold[...], HoldPattern[...] etc..\nThe actual code and trace for the above \
example follows.  This function utilizes the Non-Standard Evaluation \
procedure."
